,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":588.34297514,"data":"# Symbolic Computation (sympy):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":588.34297796,"data":"- Algebraic manipulation and simplification\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":588.34298002,"data":"- Solving equations and systems of equations\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":588.342981967,"data":"- Symbolic differentiation and integration\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":588.342983728,"data":"- Number theory functions (primes, divisors, modular arithmetic)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":588.342985481,"data":"- Polynomial operations and factorization\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":588.342987204,"data":"- Working with mathematical expressions symbolically\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":588.342989495,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":588.342991026,"data":"# Numerical Computation (numpy):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":588.342992671,"data":"- Array operations and linear algebra\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":588.342994665,"data":"- Efficient numerical calculations for large datasets\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":588.342996654,"data":"- Matrix operations and eigenvalue problems\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":588.342998459,"data":"- Statistical computations\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":588.343000276,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":588.343001647,"data":"# Mathematical Functions (math):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":588.343003338,"data":"- Standard mathematical functions (trig, log, exp)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":588.343004958,"data":"- Constants like pi and e\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":588.34300675,"data":"- Basic operations for single values\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":588.343008441,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":588.343010052,"data":"Best Practices:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":588.343011973,"data":"- Use sympy for exact symbolic answers when possible\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":588.343013834,"data":"- Use numpy for numerical verification and large-scale computation\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":588.343027238,"data":"- Combine symbolic and numerical approaches: derive symbolically, verify numerically\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":588.34302917,"data":"- Document your computational strategy clearly\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":588.343030823,"data":"- Validate computational results against known cases or theoretical bounds\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":588.343032994,"data":"- For very large exponents (e.g. a^(n!)), use pow(base, exp, mod) or analytical methods — never materialize the full number\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":588.343035687,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":588.343037426,"data":"# Code Robustness Rules:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":588.343039003,"data":"- Each code cell must be SELF-CONTAINED: re-import and re-define everything you need. If a previous cell errored, its definitions are LOST.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":588.34304109,"data":"- Avoid sympy expressions that grow beyond a few hundred characters. If an expression is exploding, switch to numerical methods (numpy) or modular arithmetic.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":588.343042933,"data":"- For geometry: prefer numpy coordinate models with brute-force verification over pure symbolic or direction-counting approaches.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":588.343044664,"data":"- For number theory / functional equations: compute small cases first (n=1..20) to find patterns before attempting a proof. Brute-force exploration often reveals the structure.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":588.343046842,"data":"- For combinatorics counting: always verify no duplicates — check injectivity explicitly.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":588.34304967,"data":"- If 5+ code cells without progress, STOP and restart with a different approach.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":588.343051347,"data":"- When using Python, prefer converting sympy expressions to int() before passing to Python builtins like pow(), min(), max().\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":588.343053127,"data":"- Common import: from sympy.ntheory.modular import crt (note: sympy.crt does not exist).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":588.343055133,"data":"- If a code cell fails, re-import necessary libraries in the next cell.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":588.343056801,"data":"- sympy.solve() often times out on complex systems. For polynomial systems with \u003e 3 unknowns, prefer numerical methods (scipy fsolve/minimize) or manual algebraic reduction.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":588.343059024,"data":"- Never call sympy.simplify() or sympy.expand() on expressions involving large binomials or products of many terms. Use float() first to check the numerical value.\n"}
